{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. You came in with chest pain this morning, right? Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. It started around 1 a.m.—a grabbing feeling in the middle of my chest. It lasted until about 9 a.m. I took nitroglycerin and it helped a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Did you have any sweating, shortness of breath, or pain going to your arm or jaw?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, just nausea. No vomiting. It felt different from my usual chest pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We did an EKG and it showed some changes, but your troponin levels—those are heart enzymes—were normal. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a heart attack?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we don’t think so. We also did a CT scan to rule out a pulmonary embolism or aortic dissection, and both were negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. But why does my chest still hurt sometimes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be related to reflux. You’ve had GERD before, right? And your heart tests don’t suggest a blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve tried omeprazole, Tums, H2 blockers—nothing really works well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep monitoring. We also noticed your blood pressure was high at home—190. We’re watching that closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s always been high. I’m on several meds for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but we noticed your pressure drops when you stand. We’re adjusting your meds—stopping atenolol and nifedipine for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I’ve been feeling a bit dizzy lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be related. We’ll keep you on carvedilol, amlodipine, and enalapril. We’ll see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my headache? It’s been bad too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You said it feels like your usual migraines. We reviewed your history—you’ve had pseudotumor cerebri with a VP shunt, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, and I’m on gabapentin now, but Tylenol doesn’t help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you oxycodone earlier, and you said it helped. We’ll use that sparingly, but it’s okay for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2141-08-19 17:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I just want the pain to stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2141-08-20 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your repeat troponins are still negative. That’s good—we’re confident it’s not a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2141-08-20 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing the chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2141-08-20 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history and the tests, it’s likely atypical chest pain, possibly from GERD. But because of your risk factors, we’re doing a stress test today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2141-08-20 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m really tired. I don’t think I can walk on a treadmill."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2141-08-20 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay. We’ll use a medication called Persantine to simulate exercise. It’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2141-08-20 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The stress test is done. You didn’t have chest pain during it, and the blood flow to your heart looked normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2141-08-20 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2141-08-20 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. There were some EKG changes, but they’re hard to interpret because of your heart’s size. Overall, no sign of blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2141-08-20 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I don’t need a stent or anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2141-08-20 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. Your prior cath showed only 50% narrowing, which isn’t severe. We’ll keep you on your heart meds like aspirin and atorvastatin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2141-08-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar has been running high—around 300. You’re on glyburide and metformin at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2141-08-21 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. My A1C was 9.5 last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2141-08-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We held your oral meds in the hospital. We’ll increase your metformin to 500 mg twice daily when you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2141-08-21 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I check my sugars more often?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2141-08-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, twice daily—fasting and after a meal. Follow up with your doctor to adjust meds if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2141-08-21 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt dizzy walking back from the bathroom. I almost fell."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2141-08-21 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked—you weren’t orthostatic. You have BPPV, right? And you’re on narcotics for headaches."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2141-08-21 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I was taught the Epley maneuver before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2141-08-21 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The dizziness is likely from the pain meds. We’re stopping the oxycodone. See how you feel tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Your dizziness is gone, blood pressure is stable, and your chest pain has improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re discharging you. We changed some meds—lower dose of nitrate, increased metformin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the chest pain? Should I worry if it comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use nitroglycerin as before. If it doesn’t help or you get shortness of breath, go to the ER. But it’s likely not heart-related."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my headache?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking gabapentin. If headaches worsen or change, contact your neurologist. Avoid narcotics if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I should quit smoking…"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s one of the best things you can do—for your heart, lungs, and diabetes. We can connect you with a counselor before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. I’m ready to try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. And use your CPAP for sleep apnea—it helps your blood pressure and heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been using it regularly. I’ll start."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing the right thing. Follow up with your PCP in a week, especially for your diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2141-08-22 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2141-08-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—what was that about the pulmonary artery on the CT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2141-08-22 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The main pulmonary artery looked a bit enlarged, which can suggest pulmonary hypertension. But it’s not new. Your primary doctor can monitor it if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2141-08-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I get more tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2141-08-22 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. It could be related to your sleep apnea or obesity. Treating those may help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2141-08-22 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll work on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2141-08-22 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on the right track. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2141-08-22 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just want to confirm—I should take the new metformin dose with food, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2141-08-22 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. With breakfast and dinner. That helps avoid stomach upset."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2141-08-22 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the nitroglycerin spray?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2141-08-22 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One spray under the tongue if chest pain occurs. Wait 5 minutes. If not better, a second. Call 911 if still no relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2141-08-22 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Understood. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2141-08-22 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re here to help. You’ll get your discharge papers soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2141-08-22 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready to go home now."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2141-08-19 16:49:00",
    "admission_end": "2141-08-22 19:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of hypertension, diabetes, migraines, obstructive sleep apnea, and a VP shunt was admitted for evaluation of atypical chest pain. Initial concern for acute coronary syndrome was ruled out by normal troponins, a negative CT angiogram for dissection or pulmonary embolism, and a stress test showing no perfusion defects. The chest pain was deemed non-cardiac, likely related to GERD, though it only partially responded to usual treatments and required morphine for relief. Her headache was consistent with her known migraines and improved with oxycodone, though narcotics were later discontinued due to dizziness likely related to BPPV and medication side effects. Blood pressure was managed by stopping atenolol and nifedipine due to orthostatic changes, continuing other antihypertensives. Diabetes was noted to be poorly controlled with persistent hyperglycemia; metformin was increased at discharge. She was counseled on smoking cessation and CPAP use, and discharged home in stable condition with follow-up plans.",
    "problems": [
      "Other chest pain",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Benign intracranial hypertension",
      "Presence of cerebrospinal fluid drainage device",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Benign paroxysmal positional vertigo",
      "Other opiates and related narcotics causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Tobacco use disorder"
    ]
  }
}
